WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.687
Around 1286, someone in Italy made the

00:00:02.697 --> 00:00:04.127
first eyeglasses.

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:06.013
And nobody wrote down his name.

00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:07.617
How do we know the date?

00:00:07.627 --> 00:00:10.451
In 1306, a friar preached in Florence:

00:00:10.551 --> 00:00:12.174
"It is not yet twenty years since

00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:13.549
this art was found.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:14.936
I saw the man who first made

00:00:14.946 --> 00:00:15.474
them."

00:00:15.484 --> 00:00:18.432
This is the oldest painting of anyone

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:19.769
wearing glasses:

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:20.979
Treviso, 1352.

00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:22.227
Look closely.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.955
Two lenses riveted together,
simply pinched onto

00:00:24.965 --> 00:00:25.856
the nose.

00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:26.431
The joke?

00:00:26.441 --> 00:00:28.898
The cardinal in the painting died in

00:00:28.908 --> 00:00:29.556
the 1260s.

00:00:29.566 --> 00:00:31.196
He never wore glasses.

00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:34.243
Later, Florence claimed
a local man, Salvino

00:00:34.253 --> 00:00:36.495
degli Armati, as the inventor.

00:00:36.505 --> 00:00:39.005
Historians call it a fraud, built in

00:00:39.015 --> 00:00:41.761
the 1600s on a faked gravestone text.

00:00:41.861 --> 00:00:44.259
The real inventor kept his secret.

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:46.022
So every pair you own goes back

00:00:46.032 --> 00:00:47.607
to a stranger in Italy...
